 (25 . "A negative amount would not match, so a refund line is silently dropped. ")
 (80 . "Here is the change I suggest, in two parts. ")
 (20 . "First, let the regexp accept an optional minus sign before the digits. ")
 (20 . "Second, make day-round handle a nil digits argument without a let binding. ")
 (20 . "Neither change touches the public functions, so callers keep working. ")
 (100 . "I ran the byte compiler on both files and it reported no warnings. ")
 (25 . "The histogram helper divides by the largest amount; with an empty ledger it uses one. ")
 (25 . "That is why it passes (apply #'max 1 amounts), and it is correct as written. ")
 (60 . "One more observation about day-average. ")
 (20 . "It returns nil for an empty ledger and a rational for a non-empty one when all amounts are integers. ")
 (20 . "Callers that format it with %f will be fine, but %d would not be. ")
 (80 . "Summary of the review so far: ")
 (20 . "the ledger is small and clear; the parser drops negative amounts; the rounding helper is sound. ")
 (20 . "I would add a test for a report containing a refund before changing anything else. ")
